      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"working-through-toxicity-and-plant-response-models\">Working through toxicity and plant-response models</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>12 November 2026 \u00b7 experimental notes</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">I am asking two different questions: <strong>Track 1</strong>, which compounds have lower\nor higher non-target toxicity? <strong>Track 2</strong>, what chemistry accompanies a\nmeasured plant response? I keep experiments (A) separate from outside-model\nestimates (B). The B models learn a teacher's estimates.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">I use <strong>F1 first</strong>. For three LD50 bins I use macro-F1, the unweighted mean\nof the three class F1 scores. For plant activity, positive means high response.\nF1 = 2TP/(2TP + FP + FN); it does not reward true negatives, so I keep the\nmajority baseline and balanced accuracy nearby.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "223783ae-b7c7-4546-9e41-07c43e93357a",
