    {
      "id": "BYtC",
      "code_hash": "6407493b228430bd9ac7d4eff08298dd",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"2-exploring-the-toxicity-classifiers\">2. Exploring the toxicity classifiers</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">I predict <strong>LD50 bin</strong>, not natural origin or herbicidal activity. Low LD50\nmeans greater acute hazard. The fixed 1,080/3,400 mg/kg cutoffs are historical\ncohort bins, not regulatory categories. Aquatic concentrations stay separate.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">I used five scaffold/connectivity-held-out folds. Scaling is fitted on each\ntraining fold. Logistic uses C=1 and balanced class weights; the forest uses\n200 trees, minimum leaf size 5 and balanced class weights. Seven predictors\ncome from structures. I have not tuned these models against the test scores.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
