    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "a145cb33c607afd8683db86a0520c51c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">My A forest reaches <strong>macro-F1 0.430</strong>, compared with majority <strong>0.226</strong>;\nlogistic is <strong>0.382</strong>. B reaches <strong>0.616</strong>, compared with majority <strong>0.200</strong>;\nlogistic is <strong>0.465</strong>. B's higher F1 describes teacher reproduction and does\nnot make it a better experimental predictor.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">I also checked continuous dose error: A forest MAE is 0.636 log10 units\nversus baseline 0.650, a small improvement. The bin result is not a reliable\ngeneral dose predictor. Nearly all paired A/B compounds overlap teacher\ntraining (3,359/3,361), so I leave combined modeling deferred.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "9be47360983fe206475687ccc5262f6a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"3-what-did-logistic-learn\">3. What did logistic learn?</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Each coefficient multiplies a <strong>one-training-fold-SD</strong> feature change in a\nclass's linear score. Positive raises that class's score; negative lowers it.\nFor multiclass relative log-odds I need the <strong>difference between two classes'\ncoefficients</strong>. These are associations among correlated features, not causes.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">I show fold means and sample SDs across five folds, not a newly fitted averaged model. Changing the\nclass below changes which score I inspect. Fold SD is variability, not a p-value.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
