    {
      "id": "qnkX",
      "code_hash": "9d39f9fcc05c0cd1e82d5a0c839bb8f2",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"5-trying-the-literature-activity-question\">5. Trying the literature activity question</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The reviewed individual policies cannot yet support five-fold activity\nmodeling. I can still inspect my earlier <strong>73-compound pooled sensitivity</strong>:\npositive = high plant response, negative = low response under source-specific\nrules. Plants, doses and endpoints differ. This is exploratory pooling.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">I compare formula logistic with fingerprint logistic/forest, keeping their\nfeature representations explicit. A high F1 needs a baseline and a new-paper\ntest: F1 alone can look good when high responses dominate.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
