        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>What I take from this:</strong> pooled fingerprint logistic F1 is 0.727 against\nmajority 0.719; forest is 0.680. All three fixed profiles have <strong>F1 = 0 on\nthe new 20-compound radish test</strong> and miss both high responses. The appealing\nwithin-pool score does not transfer. Coefficients/importance describe this\npooled experiment, not a general signature of natural herbicidal activity.\nFingerprint bits can encode multiple motifs; I cannot name a unique chemical\nmechanism from a bit number. OOB SD is not a significance test.</span>\n<h2 id=\"6-binding-evidence-stays-a-separate-experiment\">6. Binding evidence stays a separate experiment</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">I have two structural cases, tentoxin and cornexistin's bound diacid, rather\nthan a binding classifier. I can describe their exact forms, protein partners\nand contacts; there is no measured Kd/Ki training target or binding-model F1.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
